.SH NAME
sendfile \- Bundle Protocol (BP) file transmission utility utilizing a "metadata 
header" for file name, timestamp, versioning, and auxiliary command strings, 
enabling file naming at the recvfile utility. Encryption is enabled when a HMAC
key path (or literal value) is included in the command execution string.
.PP
Note: encryption requires a suitable cryptographic library and interface (which 
is avaiable with the ITAR controlled ION NASA Baseline).
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
\&\fBsendfile\fR \fIown endpoint ID\fR \fIdestination endpoint ID\fR \fIfile name\fR
[\-c|\-\-class \fIclass of service\fR] [\-t|\-\-ttl \fItime to live (seconds)\fR]
[\fIkey file path | literal key value\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
\&\fBsendfile\fR employs \fBbp_send()\fR to transmit a single bundle to a specified
destination endpoint, incorporating the file's contents detailed by
\&\fIfile_name\fR. The process concludes following the bundle's dispatch, without
initiating a custody transfer. The absence of \fIclass_of_service\fR implies a
standard priority delivery. Refer to \fBbptrace\fR\|(1) for details on
\&\fIclass_of_service\fR. Without a specified \fItime_to_live\fR, a default of 300
seconds (5 minutes) is assumed. Encryption can be facilitated by including a
valid HMAC key (either a path or a literal value) when operating within the
ITAR controlled ION NASA Baseline (ION-INB), provided a compatible
cryptographic library is installed.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.IX Header "EXIT STATUS"
.IP """0""" 4
.IX Item """0"""
Successful termination of \fBsendfile\fR.
.SH FILES
.IX Header "FILES"
No configuration files are necessary.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.IX Header "ENVIRONMENT"
Not applicable.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.IX Header "DIAGNOSTICS"
Diagnostic messages to \fBion.log\fR may include:
.IP "Can't attach to BP." 4
.IX Item "Can't attach to BP."
Signifies BP operations have yet to be initialized by \fBbpadmin\fR.
.IP "Can't open own endpoint." 4
.IX Item "Can't open own endpoint."
Indicates \fIown_endpoint_ID\fR is currently in use. Retry after the current task
has concluded or opt for a different endpoint if a previous task crashed.
.IP "Can't stat the file" 4
.IX Item "Can't stat the file"
Suggests an operating system error. Check errtext, address the issue, and
attempt the operation again.
.IP "sendfile can't create file ref." 4
.IX Item "sendfile can't create file ref."
Points to a potential critical database problem, likely requiring a reboot of
the local ION node.
.IP "sendfile can't create ZCO." 4
.IX Item "sendfile can't create ZCO."
Implies a serious database error, necessitating a restart of the ION node.
.IP "sendfile can't send file in bundle." 4
.IX Item "sendfile can't send file in bundle."
Reflects a BP system malfunction. Review earlier diagnostic messages for
possible solutions.
.SH BUGS
.IX Header "BUGS"
Report bugs to <https://github.com/nasa\-jpl/ION\-DTN/issues>.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.IX Header "SEE ALSO"
